[{"id":4341076575,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAr-SXw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Some changes are needed, but overall, I think it's going in a good direction.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [control_gallery.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28123418/control_gallery.zip)\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- In terms of UX, I think it's fine to have this defined in StyleBox. It can still be configured across a whole range of buttons using Theme resources. It roughly matches CSS behavior where you define `transition` in the styles you want to be transitioned *to* (e.g. setting `transition` on `button:hover` only affects `normal` -> `hover` transitions, not the other way around).\r\n\r\n  - Note that like in CSS, you have to be careful about transitions that try to interpolate from nothing. This can lead to artifacts with very thin outlines, for example when interpolating from no border to a 4-pixel wide border with blending enabled:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6dfa1c4c-f86c-43aa-8d66-fcda67cd0b3d\r\n\r\nOne way to avoid this is to have the border enabled with the same width and Blend property in the normal and hover states, but keep it invisible by setting its color to `Color(0, 0, 0, 0)` (transparent black):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/77f8e180-4d95-41a4-8100-0bc91ca4f615\r\n\r\nThis is probably unavoidable, but we should be careful to document this both in the class reference and manual as it'll likely come up often in support requests.\r\n\r\n- I get a crash when using an animation with the **Unset** *transition* type:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"291\" height=\"556\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9029ef94-9e96-4d21-95d2-3e5d7aff7a2b\" />\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, the **Unset** *ease* type doesn't seem to cause a crash.\r\n\r\n- Out of curiosity, what is the Unset type for? I couldn't figure it out. I assume it's meant to reuse the ease/transition type from the main animation (for the exit animation) or vice versa. What happens if both the main animation and the exit animation use the Unset type?\r\n\r\n  - If this is the intended use case of Unset, perhaps it should be renamed to Inherit and made available only on the exit animation (and made the default for the exit animation too).\r\n\r\n___\r\n\r\n@AdriaandeJongh I'm curious about your thoughts on this PR, especially considering how it would play together with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111455 for audio.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114285#pullrequestreview-4341076575","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114285","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114285#pullrequestreview-4341076575"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114285"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-21T22:16:23Z","commit_id":"760fefb4e4487fe00ea5b82d42244e125bd5db84"},{"id